<!--
  BusPulse design system: tokens and component styles. docs/DESIGN.md is the spec; this file is the implementation.

  How the tokens work
  - Every colour exists twice, as "Bp.Light.<Name>" and "Bp.Dark.<Name>": a Color for scale steps, or a string naming a
    step of the same mode for role aliases ("Neutral.12"), so a role can map to a different step in dark.
  - Views never use those. They use the alias brush "Bp.<Name>" through DynamicResource, for example
    {DynamicResource Bp.Text.Primary} or {DynamicResource Bp.Neutral.3}.
  - ThemeTokens.Apply (Themes/ThemeTokens.cs) creates the alias brushes from the Light or Dark set whenever the theme changes,
    so adding a colour means adding it to both sets here; the DesignSystemTests fail if one set misses a key.
  - Scales follow the Radix Colors 12-step model (Radix Colors 3.0.0, MIT). Steps: 1 app bg, 2 subtle bg, 3 component bg,
    4 hover, 5 pressed/selected, 6 subtle border, 7 interactive border, 8 strong border, 9 solid, 10 solid hover,
    11 low-contrast text, 12 high-contrast text.
-->
